# Bloodletter of Aclazotz: "If an opponent would lose life during your turn, they lose twice that much life instead."
# Bot1 casts it on turn 1. On Bot2's turn 2 a Lightning Bolt to Bot2 is 3 damage and 3 life lost: not Bot1's turn, so
# nothing is doubled (20 -> 17). On Bot1's turn 3 the same Bolt makes Bot2 lose 6 (17 -> 11). On that turn Bot1 itself
# pays 1 life for Marsh Flats: Bot1 is not an opponent of Bloodletter's controller, so it loses only the 1 (CR 119.4,
# 614.1a).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Bloodletter of Aclazotz
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Marsh Flats
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bloodletter of Aclazotz.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 17
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Marsh Flats.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Marsh Flats.Activate
Bot1.Search(Swamp)
? Bot1.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot2.Life = 11
